



--> ORM Basics
    What is Object Relational Mapping (ORM)?
        ORM maps:
        Java Objects ↔ Database Tables
        Instead of writing SQL:
        You work with objects
        ORM framework handles SQL internally

--> Advantages of ORM Over JDBC
        No SQL for basic operations
        Database-independent
        Less boilerplate
        Object-oriented approach
        Automatic transaction handling

--> Java Object to Table Mapping
    | Java   | Database |
    | ------ | -------- |
    | Class  | Table    |
    | Object | Row      |
    | Field  | Column   |

--> Persistence Context & Entity States
    Persistence Context = cache managed by JPA
    Entity states:
        Transient – New object, not saved
        Persistent – Managed by JPA
        Detached – Not managed anymore
        Removed – Marked for deletion
